  "body": "The drain() callback seems to work correctly, however the promise returned by drained() gets resolved before any async work has been done.\r\n\r\nExample:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nconst fastq = require('fastq');\r\n\r\n(async () => {\r\n    async function prosessTask() {\r\n      await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 0));\r\n      console.log('processed');\r\n    }\r\n    \r\n    try{\r\n      const queue = fastq.promise(prosessTask, 1); // run sequentially\r\n      queue.drain = () => console.log('called drain');\r\n      queue.drained().then( () => console.log('drained promise resolved') );\r\n    \r\n      await Promise.all([queue.push(), queue.push(), queue.push()]);\r\n    }catch(err){\r\n        console.error(err);\r\n    }\r\n})();\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe output logs I'm getting look like this:\r\n\r\n```\r\ndrained promise resolved\r\nprocessed\r\nprocessed\r\nprocessed\r\ncalled drain\r\n```\r\n\r\nI would have expected:\r\n```\r\nprocessed\r\nprocessed\r\nprocessed\r\ncalled drain\r\ndrained promise resolved\r\n```\r\n",
